{"result":"{
  "id": "19212",
  "key": "SFCC-749",
  "summary": "Breadcrumb and SEO – PWA Kit Component",
  "description": "**As a** Shopper, I want to see a breadcrumb on every page and relevant SEO text on category pages, so that I can understand where I am on the site and access additional content about the category I'm browsing.\n\nThis story covers the PWA Kit component build for the breadcrumb and SEO text component that renders above the footer. The component consumes the Contentful content type defined in SFCC-748.\n\n  - **Breadcrumb*\nThe breadcrumb renders on every page and is programmatically generated from the current page context (e.g. HOME / COLLECTIONS / RTW). No Contentful authoring is required. Rules can be applied to control breadcrumb display on certain page types — open item: Dani to share Sparro templates.\n\n**SEO Text — Collapsed State**\n\n- On category and sub-category pages, an optional SEO text block renders next to the breadcrumb showing a title and intro text fetched from Contentful, keyed by category ID. If no Contentful entry exists for that category, the SEO text block does not render.\n\n**SEO Text — Expanded State**\n\n- If an expanded SEO body is configured in Contentful for that category, a READ MORE link renders below the intro text. Clicking READ MORE reveals the full SEO body content inline. Clicking READ LESS collapses the panel back to the default state. This applies to all category and sub-category pages.\n\n**UI Design Kit:** [https://www.figma.com/design/wPiWmZZOVKnrENUWk2XWWm/Zimmermann*Design*System*2026?node-id=2083-54022&p=f&t=8DrHJtkYe3Taw9hz-0](https://www.figma.com/design/wPiWmZZOVKnrENUWk2XWWm/Zimmermann*Design*System*2026) \n\n![\"image-20260817-002936.png\"](image-20260817-002936.png)\n\nExpanded State: [https://www.figma.com/design/QQ427wHWEUjsjP7H8v48Rs/Zimmermann*Designs?node-id=3216-7913&t=JkL5PJpjbuJ8eDae-0](https://www.figma.com/design/QQ427wHWEUjsjP7H8v48Rs/Zimmermann*Designs)\n\n\n\n![\"image-20260830-234554.png\"](image-20260830-234554.png)",
