      "id": "18140",
      "key": "SFCC-95",
      "summary": "Read More SEO Text Block & Conditional Background",
      "description": "As a\n Shopper,\nI want\n to see contextual page information next to the breadcrumb navigation,\nso that\n I can understand where I am on the site and discover relevant content.\nContext:\nThis story covers two related UI behaviours tied to the area next to the breadcrumb navigation at the bottom of the page (below Recently Viewed).\nSEO text block:\n A set of labelled accordion sections is displayed beneath the Recently Viewed component. The sections are collapsed by default, showing only the section header. Each section can be individually expanded to reveal its SEO copy — for example, category descriptions or editorial content — and collapsed again by clicking the header. The section headings and body copy are CMS-managed in Contentful and are page-contextual; the content rendered depends on the page the shopper is on. This content is independent of the Recently Viewed component itself and is always present on the page regardless of whether Recently Viewed is rendered.\nConditional background colour:\n The Recently Viewed component has its own background colour. When the component is not rendered — for example, when the shopper has no browsing history — the SEO text block would otherwise appear against an orphaned coloured band that doesn't match the white content above it. The background colour of this section must therefore adapt: when Recently Viewed is rendered, it uses the standard component background; when Recently Viewed is not rendered, the background blends with the white section above to avoid a visual break.\nCurrent (needs redesign):\nFigma design reference:\n\n",
      "status": {
        "name": "To Do",
        "category": "To Do",
        "color": "blue-gray"
      },
