/**
 * Install (or update) the Zimmermann Environment Template into one target environment.
 *
 * Replaces the old runMigrations.mjs promotion flow. There is no more hand-rolled
 * '_migrationHistory' content type or detectDrift.mjs — Contentful tracks each
 * environment's install status/version natively via environmentTemplateInstallation,
 * and cross-environment content-type drift can't happen the way it used to since every
 * environment installs from the same versioned template.
 *
 * Usage:
 *   npm run sync:contentful                            # author the template first (buildTemplate.js)
 *   npm run install:contentful -- --target dev
 *   npm run install:contentful -- --target sit --dry-run
 *
 * If validation reports a content type that already exists in the target environment
 * but isn't managed by this template (e.g. one created by the old sync.js pipeline
 * before this template-based approach existed), the install is refused by Contentful.
 * Adopt it into the template explicitly rather than deleting it first:
 *   npm run install:contentful -- --target dev --takeover shoppableImage,otherType
